					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="section-prose">
					<p>
						The output vector for "cat" is mostly "cat" (46%) blended with "sat" (33%) and
						a smaller contribution from "The" (21%). This is the attention mechanism's whole
						job: it lets each token incorporate relevant context from other tokens. The output
						is no longer just "cat" — it's "cat, informed by sat and The."
					</p>
				</div>

				{/* Pipeline recap mini-diagram */}
				<div class="attn-pipeline-recap">
					<div class="attn-pipeline-title">Single attention head — full pipeline</div>
					<div class="attn-pipeline-flow">
						<div class="attn-pipeline-box attn-pipe-input">Input vectors</div>
						<div class="attn-pipeline-arrow">&rarr;</div>
						<div class="attn-pipeline-box attn-pipe-qkv">
